## The commands

| Command | Question |
|---|---|
| `doctor:half-b-readiness` | Are the five prerequisites measured, and does any signature contradict one? |
| `doctor:half-b-readiness --strict` | …and is the machinery READY? (exit 1 otherwise) |
| `doctor:half-b-readiness --activation-preflight` | …and may the fleet actually be enforced? (exit 2 otherwise) |
| `doctor:estate-resilience` | Levels 1/2/3, and the hardware. |
| `doctor:rollout-readiness` | Who is provisioned. |
| `doctor:fleet-readiness` | Who has walked the path. |
| `android:phase4a-pilot-readiness` | Is the bounded pilot prepared? |

A **contradiction exits 1 whether or not `--strict` was asked for.** Every other
condition describes a rollout in progress and exits 0, so the command is safe in
a deploy chain.
